(4650,2,240,'For a 64-byte address space with 16-byte pages (6-bit VA), match each virtual address component with its size.','{\"Virtual Page Number (VPN)\":\"2 bits (selects 1 of 4 pages)\",\"Offset\":\"4 bits (selects 1 of 16 bytes within a page)\",\"Virtual address 21 (binary 010101) - VPN field\":\"01 (page 1)\"}','{\"Virtual Page Number (VPN)\":\"2 bits (selects 1 of 4 pages)\",\"Offset\":\"4 bits (selects 1 of 16 bytes within a page)\",\"Virtual address 21 (binary 010101) - VPN field\":\"01 (page 1)\"}',3,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,0,4),
(4651,2,240,'Match each Page Table Entry (PTE) bit with its purpose.','{\"Valid bit\":\"Indicates whether the translation is valid; unused pages marked invalid to support sparse address spaces\",\"Dirty bit\":\"Set when a page has been written to since it was brought into memory\",\"Reference (accessed) bit\":\"Tracks whether a page has been accessed; used to identify popular pages\"}','{\"Valid bit\":\"Indicates whether the translation is valid; unused pages marked invalid to support sparse address spaces\",\"Dirty bit\":\"Set when a page has been written to since it was brought into memory\",\"Reference (accessed) bit\":\"Tracks whether a page has been accessed; used to identify popular pages\"}',3,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,0,4),
(4652,2,240,'Match each TLB-related term with its description.','{\"TLB\":\"A hardware cache of popular virtual-to-physical address translations inside the MMU\",\"TLB hit\":\"The desired translation is found in the TLB, allowing fast address resolution\",\"TLB miss\":\"The translation is absent from the TLB, requiring a page-table lookup\"}','{\"TLB\":\"A hardware cache of popular virtual-to-physical address translations inside the MMU\",\"TLB hit\":\"The desired translation is found in the TLB, allowing fast address resolution\",\"TLB miss\":\"The translation is absent from the TLB, requiring a page-table lookup\"}',3,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,0,4),
(4653,2,240,'Match each line/block of the TLB control-flow algorithm with its action.','{\"(Success, TlbEntry) = TLB_Lookup(VPN)\":\"Checks the TLB to see if a translation for the given VPN already exists\",\"PTEAddr = PTBR + (VPN * sizeof(PTE))\":\"Calculates the address of the page-table entry in memory during a TLB miss\",\"TLB_Insert(VPN, PTE.PFN, PTE.ProtectBits)\":\"Updates the TLB with the newly found translation so future accesses can hit\"}','{\"(Success, TlbEntry) = TLB_Lookup(VPN)\":\"Checks the TLB to see if a translation for the given VPN already exists\",\"PTEAddr = PTBR + (VPN * sizeof(PTE))\":\"Calculates the address of the page-table entry in memory during a TLB miss\",\"TLB_Insert(VPN, PTE.PFN, PTE.ProtectBits)\":\"Updates the TLB with the newly found translation so future accesses can hit\"}',3,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,0,4),
(4654,2,240,'An array of 10 integers spans pages VPN=06, 07, and 08. Match each access with its TLB outcome on the FIRST traversal.','{\"a[0] - first access on VPN 06\":\"TLB miss\",\"a[1] - second access, still on VPN 06\":\"TLB hit\",\"a[3] - first access on VPN 07\":\"TLB miss\"}','{\"a[0] - first access on VPN 06\":\"TLB miss\",\"a[1] - second access, still on VPN 06\":\"TLB hit\",\"a[3] - first access on VPN 07\":\"TLB miss\"}',3,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,0,4),
(4655,2,240,'Match each TLB context-switch mechanism with its description.','{\"TLB flush\":\"Sets all valid bits to 0, clearing the entire TLB on every context switch\",\"ASID (Address Space Identifier)\":\"A field in each TLB entry that tags translations with a process ID so multiple processes can share the TLB safely\",\"Wired TLB entries\":\"Permanently valid translations reserved by the OS, never evicted (used by TLB miss handlers)\"}','{\"TLB flush\":\"Sets all valid bits to 0, clearing the entire TLB on every context switch\",\"ASID (Address Space Identifier)\":\"A field in each TLB entry that tags translations with a process ID so multiple processes can share the TLB safely\",\"Wired TLB entries\":\"Permanently valid translations reserved by the OS, never evicted (used by TLB miss handlers)\"}',3,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,0,4),
(4656,2,240,'Match each TLB structural property with its explanation.','{\"Fully associative cache\":\"Any translation can reside in any TLB slot; hardware searches all entries in parallel\",\"Typical TLB size\":\"32, 64, or 128 entries\",\"MIPS TLB VPN width\":\"19 bits (user addresses occupy only half the 32-bit address space)\"}','{\"Fully associative cache\":\"Any translation can reside in any TLB slot; hardware searches all entries in parallel\",\"Typical TLB size\":\"32, 64, or 128 entries\",\"MIPS TLB VPN width\":\"19 bits (user addresses occupy only half the 32-bit address space)\"}',3,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,0,4),
(4657,2,240,'Match each page-table size reduction technique with its key idea.','{\"Bigger pages\":\"Reduces the number of PTEs but causes internal fragmentation\",\"Hybrid paging + segmentation\":\"Maintains one page table per segment so empty regions between heap and stack need no entries\",\"Multi-level page table\":\"Chops the linear page table into page-sized chunks and only allocates chunks that contain valid mappings\"}','{\"Bigger pages\":\"Reduces the number of PTEs but causes internal fragmentation\",\"Hybrid paging + segmentation\":\"Maintains one page table per segment so empty regions between heap and stack need no entries\",\"Multi-level page table\":\"Chops the linear page table into page-sized chunks and only allocates chunks that contain valid mappings\"}',3,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,0,4),
(4658,2,240,'Match each fragmentation type with its description.','{\"Internal fragmentation\":\"Wasted memory inside an allocated unit because allocation is larger than needed\",\"External fragmentation\":\"Wasted memory between allocated regions; the main problem with pure segmentation\",\"Typical page size to minimise internal fragmentation\":\"4 KB (as in x86) or 8 KB (as in SPARCv9)\"}','{\"Internal fragmentation\":\"Wasted memory inside an allocated unit because allocation is larger than needed\",\"External fragmentation\":\"Wasted memory between allocated regions; the main problem with pure segmentation\",\"Typical page size to minimise internal fragmentation\":\"4 KB (as in x86) or 8 KB (as in SPARCv9)\"}',3,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,0,4),
(4659,2,240,'Match each field in a two-level page table virtual address with its role.','{\"Page Directory Index (top bits of VPN)\":\"Indexes into the page directory to find the relevant Page Directory Entry (PDE)\",\"Page Table Index (lower bits of VPN)\":\"Indexes into the page of the page table pointed to by the PDE\",\"Offset\":\"Identifies the specific byte within the physical page\"}','{\"Page Directory Index (top bits of VPN)\":\"Indexes into the page directory to find the relevant Page Directory Entry (PDE)\",\"Page Table Index (lower bits of VPN)\":\"Indexes into the page of the page table pointed to by the PDE\",\"Offset\":\"Identifies the specific byte within the physical page\"}',3,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,0,4),
(4660,2,240,'For the 16 KB/64-byte-page example, match each translation step for VA 0x3F80 with its result.','{\"Final physical address (PFN 55, offset 0)\":\"55 x 64 + 0 = 3520 (0x0DC0)\"}','{\"Final physical address (PFN 55, offset 0)\":\"55 x 64 + 0 = 3520 (0x0DC0)\"}',3,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,0,4),
(4661,2,240,'Match each swap-space concept with its description.','{\"Swap space\":\"A dedicated disk area the OS uses to store pages not currently needed in RAM\",\"Swapped out\":\"A page copied from RAM to swap space to free a physical frame\",\"Present bit = 0\":\"Indicates the page has been moved to disk; the PTE stores the disk address instead of a PFN\"}','{\"Swap space\":\"A dedicated disk area the OS uses to store pages not currently needed in RAM\",\"Swapped out\":\"A page copied from RAM to swap space to free a physical frame\",\"Present bit = 0\":\"Indicates the page has been moved to disk; the PTE stores the disk address instead of a PFN\"}',3,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,0,4),
(4662,2,240,'Match each page-fault concept with its meaning.','{\"Page fault\":\"An exception raised when a process accesses a valid virtual page not currently in physical memory\",\"Page-fault handler\":\"OS software that locates the missing page on disk and brings it into a free physical frame\",\"Dirty victim page\":\"A page being evicted that must be written back to swap space because it was modified\"}','{\"Page fault\":\"An exception raised when a process accesses a valid virtual page not currently in physical memory\",\"Page-fault handler\":\"OS software that locates the missing page on disk and brings it into a free physical frame\",\"Dirty victim page\":\"A page being evicted that must be written back to swap space because it was modified\"}',3,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,0,4),
(4663,2,240,'Match each line of the OS page-fault handler pseudocode with its action.','{\"PFN = FindFreePhysicalPage()\":\"Searches for an available physical frame to load the missing page into\",\"DiskRead(PTE.DiskAddr, pfn)\":\"Issues the I\\/O to copy the page from swap space into the physical frame (process blocks)\",\"PTE.present = True; PTE.PFN = PFN\":\"Updates the page table entry so future accesses find the page in memory\"}','{\"PFN = FindFreePhysicalPage()\":\"Searches for an available physical frame to load the missing page into\",\"DiskRead(PTE.DiskAddr, pfn)\":\"Issues the I\\/O to copy the page from swap space into the physical frame (process blocks)\",\"PTE.present = True; PTE.PFN = PFN\":\"Updates the page table entry so future accesses find the page in memory\"}',3,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,0,4),
(4664,2,240,'Match each page-replacement policy with its eviction criterion.','{\"OPT (Optimal)\":\"Evicts the page that will be referenced furthest in the future\",\"FIFO\":\"Evicts the page that has been in memory the longest\",\"LRU\":\"Evicts the page that has not been used for the longest time\"}','{\"OPT (Optimal)\":\"Evicts the page that will be referenced furthest in the future\",\"FIFO\":\"Evicts the page that has been in memory the longest\",\"LRU\":\"Evicts the page that has not been used for the longest time\"}',3,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,0,4),
(4665,2,240,'Match each replacement policy with a key property or limitation.','{\"OPT\":\"Impractical for real systems as it requires knowledge of future page references\",\"FIFO\":\"Suffers from Belady\'s Anomaly - adding more frames can increase the miss rate\",\"Clock (second-chance) algorithm\":\"Approximates LRU using a use bit in each PTE; Linux uses an enhanced version\"}','{\"OPT\":\"Impractical for real systems as it requires knowledge of future page references\",\"FIFO\":\"Suffers from Belady\'s Anomaly - adding more frames can increase the miss rate\",\"Clock (second-chance) algorithm\":\"Approximates LRU using a use bit in each PTE; Linux uses an enhanced version\"}',3,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,0,4),
(4666,2,240,'For the OPT trace (cache=3, string: 0,1,2,0,1,3,0,3,1,2,1), match each access with its outcome.','{\"Access to page 2 (3rd access, cache={0,1})\":\"Miss - cold start; cache becomes {0,1,2}\",\"Access to page 3 (6th access, cache={0,1,2})\":\"Miss - page 2 evicted (used furthest in future); cache becomes {0,1,3}\",\"Access to page 2 (10th access, cache={0,1,3})\":\"Miss - page 3 evicted; cache becomes {0,1,2}\"}','{\"Access to page 2 (3rd access, cache={0,1})\":\"Miss - cold start; cache becomes {0,1,2}\",\"Access to page 3 (6th access, cache={0,1,2})\":\"Miss - page 2 evicted (used furthest in future); cache becomes {0,1,3}\",\"Access to page 2 (10th access, cache={0,1,3})\":\"Miss - page 3 evicted; cache becomes {0,1,2}\"}',3,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,0,4),
(4667,2,240,'AMAT = (H x TM) + (M x TD). With TM=100 ns and TD=10 ms, match each hit rate with approximate AMAT.','{\"Hit rate = 90%\":\"AMAT ~1 ms (0.9x100 ns + 0.1x10 ms)\",\"Hit rate = 99%\":\"AMAT ~100.99 us (0.99x100 ns + 0.01x10 ms)\",\"Hit rate = 100%\":\"AMAT = 100 ns (pure RAM; no disk penalty)\"}','{\"Hit rate = 90%\":\"AMAT ~1 ms (0.9x100 ns + 0.1x10 ms)\",\"Hit rate = 99%\":\"AMAT ~100.99 us (0.99x100 ns + 0.01x10 ms)\",\"Hit rate = 100%\":\"AMAT = 100 ns (pure RAM; no disk penalty)\"}',3,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,0,4),
(4668,2,240,'Match each thrashing-related concept with its description.','{\"Thrashing\":\"Condition where total working set exceeds physical memory; system spends more time swapping than computing\",\"Admission control\":\"Reducing the number of running processes so remaining ones\' working sets fit in memory\",\"OOM killer (Linux)\":\"A daemon that terminates a memory-intensive process when the system is critically oversubscribed\"}','{\"Thrashing\":\"Condition where total working set exceeds physical memory; system spends more time swapping than computing\",\"Admission control\":\"Reducing the number of running processes so remaining ones\' working sets fit in memory\",\"OOM killer (Linux)\":\"A daemon that terminates a memory-intensive process when the system is critically oversubscribed\"}',3,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,0,4),
