(5516,2,211,'Match each Page Table Entry (PTE) bit with its purpose.','{\"Valid bit\":\"Indicates whether the translation is valid; unused pages marked invalid to support sparse address spaces\",\"Dirty bit\":\"Set when a page has been written to since it was brought into memory\",\"Reference (accessed) bit\":\"Tracks whether a page has been accessed; used to identify popular pages\"}','{\"Valid bit\":\"Indicates whether the translation is valid; unused pages marked invalid to support sparse address spaces\",\"Dirty bit\":\"Set when a page has been written to since it was brought into memory\",\"Reference (accessed) bit\":\"Tracks whether a page has been accessed; used to identify popular pages\"}',3,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,0,2),
(5517,2,211,'Match each TLB-related term with its description.','{\"TLB\":\"A hardware cache of popular virtual-to-physical address translations inside the MMU\",\"TLB hit\":\"The desired translation is found in the TLB, allowing fast address resolution\",\"TLB miss\":\"The translation is absent from the TLB, requiring a page-table lookup\"}','{\"TLB\":\"A hardware cache of popular virtual-to-physical address translations inside the MMU\",\"TLB hit\":\"The desired translation is found in the TLB, allowing fast address resolution\",\"TLB miss\":\"The translation is absent from the TLB, requiring a page-table lookup\"}',3,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,0,2),
(5518,2,211,'Match each line/block of the TLB control-flow algorithm with its action.','{\"(Success, TlbEntry) = TLB_Lookup(VPN)\":\"Checks the TLB to see if a translation for the given VPN already exists\",\"PTEAddr = PTBR + (VPN * sizeof(PTE))\":\"Calculates the address of the page-table entry in memory during a TLB miss\",\"TLB_Insert(VPN, PTE.PFN, PTE.ProtectBits)\":\"Updates the TLB with the newly found translation so future accesses can hit\"}','{\"(Success, TlbEntry) = TLB_Lookup(VPN)\":\"Checks the TLB to see if a translation for the given VPN already exists\",\"PTEAddr = PTBR + (VPN * sizeof(PTE))\":\"Calculates the address of the page-table entry in memory during a TLB miss\",\"TLB_Insert(VPN, PTE.PFN, PTE.ProtectBits)\":\"Updates the TLB with the newly found translation so future accesses can hit\"}',3,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,0,2),
(5519,2,211,'An array of 10 integers spans pages VPN=06, 07, and 08. Match each access with its TLB outcome on the FIRST traversal.','{\"a[0] - first access on VPN 06\":\"TLB miss\",\"a[1] - second access, still on VPN 06\":\"TLB hit\",\"a[3] - first access on VPN 07\":\"TLB miss\"}','{\"a[0] - first access on VPN 06\":\"TLB miss\",\"a[1] - second access, still on VPN 06\":\"TLB hit\",\"a[3] - first access on VPN 07\":\"TLB miss\"}',3,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,0,2),
(5520,2,211,'Match each TLB context-switch mechanism with its description.','{\"TLB flush\":\"Sets all valid bits to 0, clearing the entire TLB on every context switch\",\"ASID (Address Space Identifier)\":\"A field in each TLB entry that tags translations with a process ID so multiple processes can share the TLB safely\",\"Wired TLB entries\":\"Permanently valid translations reserved by the OS, never evicted (used by TLB miss handlers)\"}','{\"TLB flush\":\"Sets all valid bits to 0, clearing the entire TLB on every context switch\",\"ASID (Address Space Identifier)\":\"A field in each TLB entry that tags translations with a process ID so multiple processes can share the TLB safely\",\"Wired TLB entries\":\"Permanently valid translations reserved by the OS, never evicted (used by TLB miss handlers)\"}',3,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,0,3),
(5521,2,211,'Match each TLB structural property with its explanation.','{\"Fully associative cache\":\"Any translation can reside in any TLB slot; hardware searches all entries in parallel\",\"Typical TLB size\":\"32, 64, or 128 entries\",\"MIPS TLB VPN width\":\"19 bits (user addresses occupy only half the 32-bit address space)\"}','{\"Fully associative cache\":\"Any translation can reside in any TLB slot; hardware searches all entries in parallel\",\"Typical TLB size\":\"32, 64, or 128 entries\",\"MIPS TLB VPN width\":\"19 bits (user addresses occupy only half the 32-bit address space)\"}',3,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,0,3),
(5522,2,211,'Match each page-table size reduction technique with its key idea.','{\"Bigger pages\":\"Reduces the number of PTEs but causes internal fragmentation\",\"Hybrid paging + segmentation\":\"Maintains one page table per segment so empty regions between heap and stack need no entries\",\"Multi-level page table\":\"Chops the linear page table into page-sized chunks and only allocates chunks that contain valid mappings\"}','{\"Bigger pages\":\"Reduces the number of PTEs but causes internal fragmentation\",\"Hybrid paging + segmentation\":\"Maintains one page table per segment so empty regions between heap and stack need no entries\",\"Multi-level page table\":\"Chops the linear page table into page-sized chunks and only allocates chunks that contain valid mappings\"}',3,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,0,3),
(5523,2,211,'Match each fragmentation type with its description.','{\"Internal fragmentation\":\"Wasted memory inside an allocated unit because allocation is larger than needed\",\"External fragmentation\":\"Wasted memory between allocated regions; the main problem with pure segmentation\",\"Typical page size to minimise internal fragmentation\":\"4 KB (as in x86) or 8 KB (as in SPARCv9)\"}','{\"Internal fragmentation\":\"Wasted memory inside an allocated unit because allocation is larger than needed\",\"External fragmentation\":\"Wasted memory between allocated regions; the main problem with pure segmentation\",\"Typical page size to minimise internal fragmentation\":\"4 KB (as in x86) or 8 KB (as in SPARCv9)\"}',3,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,0,3),
(5524,2,211,'Match each field in a two-level page table virtual address with its role.','{\"Page Directory Index (top bits of VPN)\":\"Indexes into the page directory to find the relevant Page Directory Entry (PDE)\",\"Page Table Index (lower bits of VPN)\":\"Indexes into the page of the page table pointed to by the PDE\",\"Offset\":\"Identifies the specific byte within the physical page\"}','{\"Page Directory Index (top bits of VPN)\":\"Indexes into the page directory to find the relevant Page Directory Entry (PDE)\",\"Page Table Index (lower bits of VPN)\":\"Indexes into the page of the page table pointed to by the PDE\",\"Offset\":\"Identifies the specific byte within the physical page\"}',3,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,0,3),
